From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:04:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] ASoC: topology: don't warn about deferred widget card
 binding

A component that loads its topology from its probe callback does so
while the card is being bound, before it is instantiated. The widgets
are then created by snd_soc_bind_card() itself once all components have
probed, which is the intended flow, yet soc_tplg_dapm_complete() warns
about it on every boot:

  snd-sc8280xp sound: ASoC: Parent card not yet available, widget card
    binding deferred

Every AudioReach platform takes this path. Report it at debug level.
---
 sound/soc/soc-topology.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-topology.c b/sound/soc/soc-topology.c
index 35cbe29..4c7d34f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-topology.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-topology.c
@@ -1315,7 +1315,7 @@ static int soc_tplg_dapm_complete(struct soc_tplg *tplg)
 	 * If so, just return success.
 	*/
 	if (!snd_soc_card_is_instantiated(card)) {
-		dev_warn(tplg->dev, "ASoC: Parent card not yet available, widget card binding deferred\n");
+		dev_dbg(tplg->dev, "ASoC: Parent card not yet available, widget card binding deferred\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
 
